Skeleton3D: skip modifier processing when no active modifier can change anything.

Every Skeleton3D gets an internal PhysicalBoneSimulator3D for compatibility, and
since animate_physical_bones defaults to true it's active. So every skeleton, with
or without physical bones, counted as having an active modifier: it advanced every
frame, and each update backed up and restored every bone's pose and ran the
modifier loop, which re-walked the bones after each modifier.

SkeletonModifier3D gets can_modify(), true by default. The simulator returns false
while no PhysicalBone3D is bound to it. The skeleton only advances, backs up and
processes modifiers that are active and can modify. One visible difference: the
idle compatibility simulator no longer emits modification_processed.

Upstream: not proposed yet. Drop when an equivalent change is in the Godot we pin.

